75184>>>// This provides a quick and simple way to create an about package for a program.
75184>>>// You need to create a message inside you client area called Activate_About.
75184>>>// Within this message you should send the message DoAbout passing needed
75184>>>// string information.
75184>>>//
75184>>>//       Procedure Activate_About
75184>>>//           Send DoAbout sTitle sVersion sCopyright sAuthor sBitmap
75184>>>//       End_Procedure
75184>>>//    where: sTitle =     Name of application. If none provided, uses caption
75184>>>//                        bar title
75184>>>//           sVersion   = Version Line. If none provided, will be blank
75184>>>//           sCopyRight = Copyright Line. If none provided, will be blank
75184>>>//           sAuthor    = Author name, blank if none provided
75184>>>//           sBitMap    = Bitmap logo. If none provided, standard VDF bitmap
75184>>>//                        is used.
75184>>>// It is expected that you will place this in your own object package. For
75184>>>// example an order about package may look like this:
75184>>>//
75184>>>//   // OrderAbout.pkg
75184>>>//   Use StdAbout.pkg
75184>>>//   Procedure Activate_About
75184>>>//      String sTitle sCopyright sVersion sAuthor
75184>>>//      Move "My Order Entry System" to sTitle
75184>>>//      Move "Version 2.1" to sVersion
75184>>>//      Move "Copyright xxxx, Super Software Inc." to sCopyright
75184>>>//      Move "John Smith"  to sAuthor
75184>>>//      Send DoAbout sTitle sVersion sCopyright sAuthor ""
75184>>>//   end_procedure
75184>>>//   // end of file.
75184>>>
