79198>>>>>    
79198>>>>>    // Attempt to make this as intuitive as possible. You cannot invoke this when a
79198>>>>>    // report is active. If a report is not finished, you cannot do this.
79198>>>>>    // If a report is finsihed it may or may not have a viewer present.
79198>>>>>    // If a viewer is not present, we will clear the exising report (making the assumption
79198>>>>>    // that a modeless viewer was closed and the report will not be invoked again). If a viewer
79198>>>>>    // is active, we will pass this through to the winprint object which will show an error
79198>>>>>    
79198>>>>>    Function DFPrintSetupDialog Returns Boolean// invoke printer setup dialog
79200>>>>>        Integer iStatus
79200>>>>>        Boolean bActiveViewer bOk
79200>>>>>        // we must have printers installed for this to work
79200>>>>>        Get ArePrintersInstalled to bOk
79201>>>>>        If not bOk Begin
79203>>>>>            Error DFERR_WINPRINT C_$NoInstalledPrinters
79204>>>>>>
79204>>>>>        End
79204>>>>>>
79204>>>>>        Else Begin
79205>>>>>            Get DocumentStatus to iStatus
79206>>>>>            If (iStatus=dsFinished) Begin
79208>>>>>                Get IsViewerActive to bActiveViewer
79209>>>>>                If not bActiveViewer Begin
79211>>>>>                    Send DfClearDoc
79212>>>>>                End
79212>>>>>>
79212>>>>>            End
79212>>>>>>
79212>>>>>            // the winprint object will generate an error if the status is not dsNotStarted.
79212>>>>>            // we want those errors
79212>>>>>            Get DFPrintSetupDialog of (phoWinPrint(Self)) to bOk
79213>>>>>        End
79213>>>>>>
79213>>>>>        Function_Return bOk
79214>>>>>    End_Function
79215>>>>>    
79215>>>>>    // It is better to use DFPrintSetupDialog which tells you if the dialog was canceled
